%N A400171 Numbers k not divisible by any p^p and for which A003415(k) is a multiple of A276085(k), where A003415 is the arithmetic derivative and A276085 is the primorial base log-function.
%C A400171 Sequence A276086(A351087(.)) sorted into ascending order, thus 21759362625, 39062920050, 47522447973, 125375375125, 215396351625, 759556778750, 1248987546730, 1595069235375, etc. are also terms, but it should be checked that there are no any other terms between. In general, the terms seem to have quite compact factorization (that is, difference A061395(k)-A001221(k) stays small, see A351087).
%C A400171 Conjecture: For all terms k > 1, A008966(k) = A063524(A003415(k)/A276085(k)), i.e., the quotient is 1 if and only if k is squarefree.
%F A400171 {k such that A359550(k) = 1 and A003415(k) = e*A276085(k) for some e >= 1}.
%F A400171 {k such that A359550(k) = 1 and A276085(A380459(k)) = A276085(k^e) for some e >= 1}.
%o A400171 (PARI) is_A400171(k) = (A359550(k) && A373489(k));
%Y A400171 Intersection of A048103 and A373490. Subsequence of A400172.
%Y A400171 Cf. A003415, A008966, A063524, A276085, A276086, A351087, A359550, A373489, A380459.
%K A400171 nonn,more,changed
